// The mesh module's public surface: build both flattened lists once at
// startup (meshbuild/), and report how many triangles they hold (12 cols-1 *
// 39 rows-1 * 2 = 936, the "count" gl_draw_tris wants) -- same shape as
// demos/gl3d/scene/mesh/api.id. The terrain never changes after this, so the
// per-frame cost is just rebuilding the camera matrices (flight/), not
// rebuilding geometry.

mesh_init() {
  build_verts();
  build_colors();
} return void;

tri_count() {
} return int 936;
